So I'm playing a new droven wizard, lvl 5, goes by the name of Junkie.
Down to the 4th level of the Mines, I've pretty much cleared out the
level, except for some snakes and a bee.  Down to last one that I can
see, so, though I had low HP and was out of magic, I went after the bee
with my quarterstaff.  Bad series of turns of straightforward
attacking, and it has me down to 3 HP.  No other healing option, I
quaff my blessed potion of extra healing.  This is a potion was a
starting item, identified and all.

And out pops a Djinni.  I'm profoundly excited for about half a second
before I realize the true nature and extent of my predicament.  Not
seeing anyway out of it, I ask for an amulet of lifesaving.  And,
naturally, before I get another turn to equip it, before the Djinni's
even disappeared from the screen: DYWYPI.

So, o' more experienced Slashem users, what the hell happened?  Glad
though I was for a wish, why was my potion, preidentified as a "blessed
potion of extra healing", actually a djinni in a bottle?  I haven't
seen this possibility noted in any spoiler.  And, fortuitous though it
might otherwise be, it effectively killed my poor Junkie, here.



